00:16:14,512 --> 00:16:16,512
One night

250
00:16:16,512 --> 00:16:18,512
Takashi was living alone in his apartment

251
00:16:18,512 --> 00:16:21,512
Takashi was home alone.

252
00:16:22,512 --> 00:16:23,512
What?

253
00:16:24,464 --> 00:16:26,464
You really called?

254
00:16:26,464 --> 00:16:27,464
Really.

255
00:16:27,464 --> 00:16:29,464
It was Midsummer calling.

256
00:16:29,464 --> 00:16:32,464
Can I go to Takashi's now?

257
00:16:32,464 --> 00:16:36,464
He said he'd be there in half an hour.

258
00:16:36,464 --> 00:16:40,464
So Takashi waited at home.

259
00:16:40,464 --> 00:16:45,464
But 30 minutes passed, and Mafuyu still hadn't arrived.

260
00:16:45,464 --> 00:16:47,464
I wonder what's wrong.

261
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:50,464
Maybe the train is late.

262
00:16:50,464 --> 00:16:52,464
I wondered...

263
00:16:53,168 --> 00:16:56,168
Wow! What a surprise! What is it?

264
00:16:57,168 --> 00:17:01,168
I heard a pounding on the front door.

265
00:17:02,168 --> 00:17:05,168
What's that? I wondered why the intercom wasn't ringing.

266
00:17:06,168 --> 00:17:09,168
I wondered if the intercom was broken.

267
00:17:09,168 --> 00:17:11,168
I was about to go to the front door.

268
00:17:12,168 --> 00:17:13,168
Oh, what a surprise!

269
00:17:15,168 --> 00:17:17,168
I got another call.

270
00:17:18,168 --> 00:17:22,168
What's wrong? Midwinter. I said I'd open the front door now.

271
00:17:23,120 --> 00:17:24,680
Don't open the door!

272
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:28,760
A woman on all fours, dressed all in black, just now climbed up on the front porch.

273
00:17:28,760 --> 00:17:30,680
She was banging on the Takashin's door.

274
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,680
What?

275
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:35,120
She climbed up on the roof and went to the balcony.

276
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:36,480
Takashi?

277
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:37,280
What?

278
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,280
I thought, "What?

279
00:17:38,672 --> 00:17:41,672
And when he looked back at the window, there it was!

280
00:17:41,672 --> 00:17:43,672
Wow! That's scary.

281
00:17:43,672 --> 00:17:47,672
Scary! Ow! Ow!

282
00:17:47,672 --> 00:17:49,672
Ow!

283
00:17:49,672 --> 00:17:52,672
Whoa! Okay, okay!

284
00:17:52,672 --> 00:17:54,672
Whoa!

285
00:17:54,672 --> 00:17:57,672
No, rap, rap.

286
00:17:57,672 --> 00:18:02,672
Hey, no, no, wait, no! No! No! No! No! A little more!

287
00:18:02,672 --> 00:18:05,672
What? Watch out! Look out!

288
00:18:06,672 --> 00:18:08,672
What the hell?

289
00:18:08,672 --> 00:18:10,672
I'm scared.

290
00:18:11,584 --> 00:18:15,584
That's all. I thought it was over.

291
00:18:15,584 --> 00:18:19,584
I'm too scared. What? Neither of you are crying.

292
00:18:19,584 --> 00:18:23,584
What's wrong? Are you scared all of a sudden?

293
00:18:23,584 --> 00:18:28,584
Tears in my eyes, but they haven't fallen yet.

294
00:18:28,584 --> 00:18:32,584
Now, the last plan! Still no plan?

295
00:18:32,584 --> 00:18:36,584
I brought a present for Manassa at the end. A present?

296
00:18:36,584 --> 00:18:39,584
I'm scared of presents with this tone.

297
00:18:39,584 --> 00:18:43,584
I thought it would be perfect for Manassa, so I asked her to open it.

298
00:18:44,944 --> 00:18:48,186
 Hanya.

299
00:18:48,186 --> 00:18:54,506
My father's graduation present was a mannequin head for haircuts.

300
00:18:54,506 --> 00:18:57,506
What are you doing?

301
00:18:57,506 --> 00:19:00,506
Wow! You scared me!Wow! You scared me! 

302
00:19:00,506 --> 00:19:05,506
Isn't she scary as hell?

303
00:19:05,506 --> 00:19:08,506
Was she like that?

304
00:19:08,506 --> 00:19:11,506
Oh, my God!

305
00:19:11,506 --> 00:19:17,506
Akimoto manages to keep her tears from spilling, and is attacked by her horror father!

306
00:19:17,826 --> 00:19:20,826
And here comes the counterattack!

307
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:24,826
I heard that Ayume might meet you today.

308
00:19:24,826 --> 00:19:27,826
I brought something for you, too.

309
00:19:27,826 --> 00:19:30,826
It's in here.

310
00:19:30,826 --> 00:19:35,826
We did a tour in the summer, and it's been three years since you've been on the road.

311
00:19:35,826 --> 00:19:38,826
Akimoto wants to make you cry no matter what it takes.

312
00:19:38,826 --> 00:19:43,826
Akimoto, who wanted to cry no matter what, completed the gold tape message operation he used to welcome us here again.

313
00:19:44,146 --> 00:19:48,146
He's always there to support the group, and I can always feel it.

314
00:19:48,146 --> 00:19:51,146
I can always feel it.

315
00:19:51,146 --> 00:19:54,146
I'm sure you have a lot of thoughts and difficulties, but you don't say them to others.

316
00:19:54,146 --> 00:19:58,146
But you don't talk about it to others.

317
00:19:58,146 --> 00:20:01,146
You're the youngest member of the group.

318
00:20:01,146 --> 00:20:04,146
I think it's cool that you have such strength.

319
00:20:04,146 --> 00:20:07,146
I really respect you as a person.

320
00:20:07,146 --> 00:20:09,146
Are you okay?

321
00:20:09,146 --> 00:20:11,146
I want you to keep it.

322
00:20:11,146 --> 00:20:13,146
Akimoto, you got them all.

323
00:20:13,466 --> 00:20:15,466
Thank you.

324
00:20:15,466 --> 00:20:18,466
I'll put my power in it.

325
00:20:18,466 --> 00:20:20,466
Thank you very much.

326
00:20:20,466 --> 00:20:22,466
Only Tsutsui failed.

327
00:20:24,466 --> 00:20:29,466
Tsutsui's horror plan failed and too many tears flowed

328
00:20:29,466 --> 00:20:32,466
Akimoto's golden tape freedom ceremony brought tears to my eyes.

329
00:20:32,466 --> 00:20:35,466
She made everyone cry.

330
00:20:39,466 --> 00:20:42,466
Why are you trying to make us cry with that?

331
00:20:42,786 --> 00:20:46,786
I wanted to go in a different direction from everyone else

332
00:20:46,786 --> 00:20:49,786
I thought everyone would come from different directions.

333
00:20:49,786 --> 00:20:51,786
I thought everyone was coming from different directions, but it was just the emotional ones.

334
00:20:51,786 --> 00:20:53,786
It's like I'm the weird one.

335
00:20:54,786 --> 00:20:57,786
When that scary story starts, I just keep laughing.

336
00:20:57,786 --> 00:21:00,786
I know what I'm talking about, so I'm laughing... more and more.

337
00:21:00,786 --> 00:21:04,786
I thought they were trying to make me cry.

338
00:21:04,786 --> 00:21:06,786
It's funny all the time.

339
00:21:06,786 --> 00:21:08,786
That paper.

340
00:21:08,786 --> 00:21:10,786
I'm sorry to all the people I gave it to.

341
00:21:11,106 --> 00:21:13,106
I gave it to someone else.

342
00:21:13,106 --> 00:21:15,106
I gave one to Ume too.

343
00:21:15,106 --> 00:21:18,106
But it seemed like I wasn't the only one who got it.

344
00:21:18,106 --> 00:21:20,106
I got the feeling that you just found out about it.

345
00:21:20,106 --> 00:21:23,106
I was just watching the video, thinking what if it's the same sentence now?

346
00:21:23,106 --> 00:21:25,106
You were just wrong.

347
00:21:25,106 --> 00:21:27,106
It wasn't.

348
00:21:27,106 --> 00:21:29,106
It didn't sound canned.

349
00:21:29,106 --> 00:21:31,106
That's a good point.

350
00:21:31,106 --> 00:21:33,106
It wasn't canned.

351
00:21:33,106 --> 00:21:38,106
And to Akimoto and the member who made him cry, a reward for this project.

352
00:21:38,426 --> 00:21:41,426
When I said we talked about canulés.

353
00:21:41,426 --> 00:21:44,426
Patisserie Parola!

354
00:21:44,426 --> 00:21:46,426
Patisserie Parola!

355
00:21:46,426 --> 00:21:47,426
Cannoulet.

356
00:21:47,426 --> 00:21:49,426
They're so good!

357
00:21:49,426 --> 00:21:54,426
Your reward is a canulé made with French fermented butter, which Bananaman recommended earlier.

358
00:21:54,426 --> 00:21:56,426
Patisserie Parola's canele!

359
00:21:56,426 --> 00:21:59,426
After making 8 people cry, Akimoto got 8 canulés!

360
00:22:01,426 --> 00:22:03,426
They are so good!

361
00:22:03,426 --> 00:22:05,426
350 yen per piece!

362
00:22:05,746 --> 00:22:07,746
High quality!

363
00:22:08,746 --> 00:22:11,746
After making Akimoto cry, he tried to eat the canele!

364
00:22:11,746 --> 00:22:13,746
They are so delicious!

365
00:22:13,746 --> 00:22:15,746
It's so good, I can't stop staring at it!

366
00:22:15,746 --> 00:22:17,746
I'm just staring at it

367
00:22:17,746 --> 00:22:19,746
This is so good!

368
00:22:20,746 --> 00:22:22,746
It's so good, isn't it?

369
00:22:22,746 --> 00:22:24,746
It's my favorite type of canele!

370
00:22:24,746 --> 00:22:26,746
I'm so grateful. Let me try a little something.

371
00:22:26,746 --> 00:22:28,256
It's so good!

372
00:22:29,256 --> 00:22:35,256
I'm sorry about the planning of this event, but Akimoto knew about it, too.

373
00:22:35,256 --> 00:22:40,256
It was a surprise in reverse, but from this point on, even Akimoto didn't know about it.

374
00:22:40,256 --> 00:22:41,256
What?

375
00:22:42,256 --> 00:22:45,256
I received a letter.

376
00:22:45,256 --> 00:22:46,256
Who is it?

377
00:22:47,256 --> 00:22:49,256
I'd like to read it for you.

378
00:22:49,256 --> 00:22:50,256
Yes, sir.

379
00:22:51,344 --> 00:22:54,304
Go for it, eh?

380
00:22:54,304 --> 00:23:01,184
Congratulations on your graduation. At first, I was worried about entering this world and was against it, but now...

381
00:23:01,184 --> 00:23:13,384
I've been so happy to be a part of this wonderful group called Nogizaka46. I've decided for years that my last summer tour would be a nationwide tour, so last year's tour was a great opportunity for me to go all over the country with my dad.

382
00:23:13,384 --> 00:23:20,784
You went all over the country with my dad. When I saw fans, I thanked them from the bottom of my heart.

383
00:23:20,784 --> 00:23:30,864
You have a long life ahead of you after you graduate from Nogizaka46. Nacchan is a girl who has her own ideas, so please believe in yourself and keep going.

384
00:23:30,864 --> 00:23:41,904
I'll protect you no matter what happens, and I know I'm not always there to help you, but you can tell me anything. I'll talk to you a lot more from now on.

385
00:23:42,784 --> 00:23:45,264
Here's a cannulator for you, Mommy.

386
00:23:45,264 --> 00:23:49,424
Thank you, Mom. What a surprise!

387
00:23:49,424 --> 00:23:57,944
I was really surprised.

388
00:23:57,944 --> 00:24:02,144
It's going to be like it's the last one today.

389
00:24:02,144 --> 00:24:06,544
There's still a few more shows to go.

390
00:24:06,544 --> 00:24:12,464
What's with all the crying?

